From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sobs <antohasobne@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 18:35:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] quartz: IMediaPosition times at the x87 precision of the
 caller.

Swashbucklers plays a movie until its position, kept as a float, is not
below the duration, a double (AGL.dll 0x10032ac9). At the end the filter
graph gives the position equal to the duration, 19.16 s for its logo
movie, and float 19.16 is 19.1599998: the game never left the logo's
loop, and the screen stayed black where the intro should have played
(A or B skipped to the menu).

Native quartz divides on the x87, whose precision control Direct3D sets
to 24 bits on the thread that makes the device (unless
D3DCREATE_FPU_PRESERVE; the game's flags are 0x50): both times then
have a float's precision and compare equal. This build divides with
SSE2, which the control word does not touch. Round the REFTIME results
to a float when the control word asks for 24 bits.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 dlls/quartz/filtergraph.c | 22 +++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/quartz/filtergraph.c b/dlls/quartz/filtergraph.c
--- a/dlls/quartz/filtergraph.c
+++ b/dlls/quartz/filtergraph.c
@@ -2663,6 +2663,25 @@
     return S_OK;
 }
 
+/* Native quartz converts with the x87, whose precision control the calling
+ * thread may have lowered: Direct3D sets it to 24 bits unless the device is
+ * made with D3DCREATE_FPU_PRESERVE. Its times then have a float's precision,
+ * and programs rely on it: Swashbucklers keeps a movie's position as a float
+ * and plays the movie until that is not below the duration, a double, which
+ * an exact 19.16 never reaches (19.1599998 < 19.16). This build divides with
+ * SSE, which the control word does not touch: round as the x87 would. */
+static REFTIME reftime_at_fpu_precision(REFTIME time)
+{
+#if defined(__i386__) && (defined(__GNUC__) || defined(__clang__))
+    WORD cw;
+
+    __asm__ volatile ("fnstcw %0" : "=m" (cw));
+    if (!(cw & 0x300))
+        return (float)time;
+#endif
+    return time;
+}
+
 static HRESULT ConvertToREFTIME(IMediaSeeking *seek, LONGLONG time_in, REFTIME *time_out)
 {
     GUID time_format;
@@ -2677,7 +2696,8 @@
         return E_NOTIMPL;
     }
 
-    *time_out = (REFTIME)time_in / 10000000; /* convert from 100 ns intervals to 1 second intervals */
+    /* convert from 100 ns intervals to 1 second intervals */
+    *time_out = reftime_at_fpu_precision((REFTIME)time_in / 10000000);
     return S_OK;
 }
 
